Falsifies `system_tests::user::confinement_attack_tests::a_read_only_holder_cannot_send_and_an_ungranted_slot_names_nothing`.

Architecture: aarch64

The patch deletes the `WRITE` check on `Rendezvous::SEND` in `syscall::invoke`, so a holder of
`READ` alone sends: the right the capability lacks is taken from the method number instead, which
is claim 2's "userspace cannot forge a right" at the dispatcher, on the IPC fastpath of §10 (the
capability-based microkernel process model). A receiver is already parked, so
the broken gate delivers rather than blocking.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!` "a READ-only holder SENT: WRITE was forged from the method or an
argument register". Replayed on 2026-10-06 (UTC) by the milestone 633 (an outside agent attacks the
confinement claim) lane: red at exactly that assertion on aarch64.

